{
  "title": "Mean platelet volume does not improve frozen cross-cycle log-CRP prediction beyond standard blood-count correlates",
  "abstract": "In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, adding mean platelet volume splines to a source-only-trained model containing platelet count, leukocyte differential, albumin, BMI and demographics did not improve frozen prediction of log CRP in the separately sampled 2007\u201308 cycle: weighted MSE gain -0.001028 (target-PSU conditional-source 95% interval -0.003125 to 0.001187; n=4871). This is a bounded negative prediction result, not evidence that MPV has no biological association.",
